From 983fd7616f3c523db5892eef9d19b130a0c5d5b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:26:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www, others: dashboard IPv6 live, IPv6 pages, Firewall apply
 that answers the first click, Survey CSV guard, diag v1.3.33

- Dashboard: the Internet card's IPv6 half is re-read on every poll (it was
  painted once at load), polls fast while IPv6 is configured but not yet up.
- Connections, Devices, Traffic, DNS Failover (IPv6 status line, reverse DNS and
  IPv6-name switches), Advisor (IPv6 endpoint), Warden (IPv4-only chip): IPv6.
- Firewall: Apply/Keep/Revert dim at once and poll until the router reports the
  state, so the first click is not refused as a double apply.
- Devices: the table card sizes to its rows instead of clipping its last column.
- Network editor: the per-network IPv6 switch stays on screen for wired-only
  VLANs.
- Site Survey CSV: a value starting with = + - @ tab or CR is exported as text
  (audit V10).
- www/Makefile: the dangling /www/fb_data.tgz.gz* links into /tmp are gone
  (audit V5); ASUS's app-installer test form is not shipped (V11).
- Hard-coded English replaced by dictionary tokens on three pages.
- reaper_diag v1.3.32-v1.3.33: per-network IPv6, the health check per family,
  the tunnel, reverse DNS and IPv6 names; the /tmp hardening; the dynamic
  puncturing gain and interval actually applied; scratch files private, report
  created fresh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
